{"id":"h11t3","name":"Monthly Shipments in EUR","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>shipments</b> has the columns <code>shipment_id</code>, <code>shipped_on</code> (date), <code>currency</code> and <code>amount</code>. The table <b>fx_rates</b> has the columns <code>currency</code>, <code>rate_date</code> (date) and <code>rate_to_eur</code>. Rates are not published every day.</p>\n<p>Currency codes in <b>shipments</b> were typed by hand: they can be in lower case or padded with spaces (<code>' usd'</code> is <code>USD</code>). Codes in <b>fx_rates</b> are clean.</p>\n<p>A shipment is converted to EUR with the <b>latest rate of its currency published on or before</b> its <code>shipped_on</code> date. <code>EUR</code> shipments use the rate 1 (there is no EUR row in <b>fx_rates</b>). A shipment with no rate available is <b>unconverted</b>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return one row per month (the first day of the month of <code>shipped_on</code>, as a date) with the columns <code>month</code>, <code>shipments</code> (number of converted shipments), <code>total_eur</code> and <code>avg_eur</code> (sum and average of the converted amounts, rounded to 2 decimals, <code>NULL</code> when nothing was converted), <code>unconverted</code> and <code>top_currency</code> (the clean currency code with the highest converted total that month; on a tie, the first code in alphabetical order; <code>NULL</code> when nothing was converted), sorted by <code>month</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>shipments</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>shipment_id</th><th>shipped_on</th><th>currency</th><th>amount</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-01-05</td><td>usd</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-01-10</td><td> USD </td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2026-01-11</td><td>EUR</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2026-01-02</td><td>GBP</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>2026-02-03</td><td>gbp</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2026-02-04</td><td>MAD</td><td>1000</td></tr></table></div><p>Table <code>fx_rates</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>currency</th><th>rate_date</th><th>rate_to_eur</th></tr><tr><td>USD</td><td>2026-01-01</td><td>0.9</td></tr><tr><td>USD</td><td>2026-01-10</td><td>0.8</td></tr><tr><td>GBP</td><td>2026-01-03</td><td>1.2</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>month</th><th>shipments</th><th>total_eur</th><th>avg_eur</th><th>unconverted</th><th>top_currency</th></tr><tr><td>2026-01-01</td><td>3</td><td>250.0</td><td>83.33</td><td>1</td><td>USD</td></tr><tr><td>2026-02-01</td><td>1</td><td>120.0</td><td>120.0</td><td>1</td><td>GBP</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>shipments</code>, <code>fx_rates</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>month</code>, <code>shipments</code>, <code>total_eur</code>, <code>avg_eur</code>, <code>unconverted</code>, <code>top_currency</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["jointure « as-of »","LATERAL","nettoyage de codes","DISTINCT ON","COUNT(col) vs COUNT(*)"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>shipments</code>, <code>fx_rates</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 6 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>month</code>, <code>shipments</code>, <code>total_eur</code>, <code>avg_eur</code>, <code>unconverted</code>, <code>top_currency</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; une case vide attendue s'écrit <code>null</code> : ce n'est ni <code>0</code> ni une chaîne vide ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 9 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"shipments":{"columns":[["shipment_id","INT"],["shipped_on","DATE"],["currency","TEXT"],["amount","NUMERIC(12,2)"]],"rows":[[1,"2026-01-05","usd",100],[2,"2026-01-10"," USD ",50],[3,"2026-01-11","EUR",120],[4,"2026-01-02","GBP",10],[5,"2026-02-03","gbp",100],[6,"2026-02-04","MAD",1000]]},"fx_rates":{"columns":[["currency","TEXT"],["rate_date","DATE"],["rate_to_eur","NUMERIC(12,6)"]],"rows":[["USD","2026-01-01",0.9],["USD","2026-01-10",0.8],["GBP","2026-01-03",1.2]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["month","shipments","total_eur","avg_eur","unconverted","top_currency"],"rows":[["2026-01-01",3,250.0,83.33,1,"USD"],["2026-02-01",1,120.0,120.0,1,"GBP"]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"shipments":{"columns":[["shipment_id","INT"],["shipped_on","DATE"],["currency","TEXT"],["amount","NUMERIC(12,2)"]],"rows":[[1,"2026-03-01","xof",6559.57],[2,"2026-04-01","EUR",10],[3,"2026-04-02","eur",10]]},"fx_rates":{"columns":[["currency","TEXT"],["rate_date","DATE"],["rate_to_eur","NUMERIC(12,6)"]],"rows":[["XOF","2026-03-02",0.001524]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["month","shipments","total_eur","avg_eur","unconverted","top_currency"],"rows":[["2026-03-01",0,null,null,1,null],["2026-04-01",2,20.0,10.0,0,"EUR"]]}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":""}